 "summary_tex": "From $\\langle\\mu\\rangle=0$ to 50 the reco selection efficiency of $t\\bar t$ goes from 20\\% to 28\\% (pileup jets pass the $\\geq4$-jet cut; the card has no pileup-jet rejection), the mean jet multiplicity from 3.7 to 4.4, the fraction of events with all four $\\chi^2$ jets correct from 18\\% to 5.8\\%, and the neutrino $p_z$ half-width from 65 to 92~GeV.  The $hh$ separation of the masses goes from AUC 0.616 to 0.540 and that of angles + masses from 0.617 to 0.538; the gen-level check is 0.698, 0.698 at the three pileup levels, as it must be for paired events that do not see pileup at gen level."
